## 2. Reproduction: the 14 [ce] cases through all 25 deploy-path odds steps at 323990ea (checkers unchanged)
##    X1 was then rewritten on one line (its first form was red for an incidental reason) and rerun from
##    a worktree fixed at 4827946e (checkers identical to 323990ea).

deploy.yml at 323990ea: running 25 odds steps of the 96 runnable steps (no secret) before "Deploy to Cloudflare Workers":
  - Every odds call is charged to the monthly ledger
  - a degrade-open names its error and counts it by reason
  - a batch and the helper reading it agree on their statement count
  - the odds-live 404 path returns before the charge
  - the odds budget schema is on ARCHIVE_DB and readable from CI
  - the monthly charge is atomic and its ceiling binds
  - the monthly odds counter has not grown another non-atomic writer
  - a ceiling veto is readable from /budget/odds
  - the odds budget batch keeps its order and its ceilings
  - The backfill cannot pay for a payload and pair none of it
  - the WC lambda call stays gated, and the sport list stays one list
  - reconcile counts every call once, with no read
  - every table a script creates is on the /d1/execute allow-list
  - One team-name matcher, and it can fail
  - Every odds call names which consumer spent it
  - Every charged odds call is reconciled against the receipt
  - Consumers read the last PRE-KICKOFF price, not the closing column
  - The backfill logs only writes it actually made
  - the odds-key tables are one table, and unchanged by the move
  - closing_odds is not pre-filled for unplayed games
  - no writer can stamp a post-kickoff price as the close
  - every odds writer fetches its own sport's payload
  - a budget grant cannot outlive its day
  - soccer h2h yields a draw, and no other market gains one
  - no opening line is written onto a finished game

